      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md#provenance-41",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Guardrails",
      "prov:value": "Six observations on this repository\n  between 2026-09-19 and 2026-09-20: a push, a PR opened shortly after, and\n  **no `pull_request`-event run ever fires for that head**.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19",
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md#provenance-42",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Guardrails",
      "prov:value": "**Read `mergeable_state` FIRST — and believe it only when it says\n     `dirty`.** `clean` and `unknown` are not evidence here: `fx5r` measured\n     the PR endpoint serving a merged PR's pre-merge view for 45 minutes, and\n     `unknown` means GitHub has not finished computing it (`h2s9`)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md#provenance-43",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "Guardrails",
      "prov:value": "Measured on\n     PR #715, 2026-09-21: the conflicting commit reached `main` 27 minutes\n     BEFORE the PR was opened, zero runs fired for that head, and CI fired\n     immediately once the base was merged in and the conflict resolved.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#715",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md#provenance-44",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Guardrails",
      "prov:value": "That is the workaround every one of the six needed; it is written here\n     rather than left as folklore (`3pqn` Done-when 3).\n  4."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md#provenance-45",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "Guardrails",
      "prov:value": "A new commit moves the head, and the head is\n     what the absence attaches to — measured on PR #552, which hit this twice in\n     eight minutes, on two different commits.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#552"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md#provenance-46",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Guardrails",
      "prov:value": "**Why this sits under a guardrail rather than in the recipe.** An agent\n  holding a standing merge authorisation will read zero checks as nothing-red\n  and merge unverified."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md#provenance-47",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Guardrails",
      "prov:value": "That is not a hypothetical either: the session that\n  wrote this rule was operating under exactly such an authorisation when #552\n  reproduced the bug, and was one step from merging a PR with no coverage at\n  all.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#552"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md#provenance-48",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Guardrails",
      "prov:value": "A merged branch is still the record of how the work was done, the\n  base a revert or a follow-up is cut from, and the ref a staging deploy is served\n  under; deleting it is irreversible from the agent's side and buys nothing the\n  owner asked for."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md#provenance-49",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Guardrails",
      "prov:value": "**This is stated in [`prepare-merge-auto.md`](prepare-merge-auto.md) too** —\n  Phase 4 step 4 and Phase 5 — and it was stated there *only*, which is how it got\n  broken."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md#provenance-50",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Guardrails",
      "prov:value": "`AGENTS.md` §More, \"Shipping a branch\", points at THIS file, so an agent that\n  followed the pointer never met the rule: measured 2026-09-19, a session proposed\n  \"deleting the branch after each merge\" as a way to stop a stop-hook false\n  positive.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
